    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Experimental Results\n",
        "\n",
        "### Charitable Contribution Made\n",
        "\n",
        "First, I analyze whether matched donations lead to an increased response rate of making a donation. \n"
      ],
      "id": "43d6b6e9"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "# Calculate group means\n",
        "donation_rates = df.groupby('treatment')['gave'].mean()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Plot\n",
        "plt.bar(['Control', 'Treatment'], donation_rates)\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Proportion Donated')\n",
        "plt.title('Donation Rate by Group')\n",
        "plt.ylim(0, 0.03)  # Adjust for visibility\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "837bdd24",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "A statistical comparison using a t-test showed that this difference is **statistically significant**, with a p-value of **0.013**:"
      ],
      "id": "0c22f40e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#|echo: false\n",
        "gave_treat = df[df['treatment'] == 1]['gave']\n",
        "gave_ctrl = df[df['treatment'] == 0]['gave']\n",
        "ttest3 = stats.ttest_ind(gave_treat, gave_ctrl, equal_var=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"{'Statistic':<12} {'Value'}\")\n",
        "print(f\"{'-'*25}\")\n",
        "print(f\"{'t-statistic':<12} {ttest3.statistic:.4f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"{'p-value':<12} {ttest3.pvalue:.4f}\")"
      ],
      "id": "abc15345",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "In plain terms, this means that the difference in donation behavior is **unlikely to be due to chance**. \n",
        "\n",
        " Even though the financial difference is small, simply **framing a donation opportunity with a matching offer** significantly increased the likelihood that people would give. This supports the idea that donors respond not just to financial incentives, but to **social framing and perceived impact**. When people feel their donation is part of something larger — like a matching challenge — they may be more likely to act.\n",
        "\n",
        "##### Probit Regression:"
      ],
      "id": "e28767bf"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#|echo: false\n",
        "# Probit regression\n",
        "model_probit = smf.probit('gave ~ treatment', data=df).fit()\n",
        "model_probit.summary()"
      ],
      "id": "45d60a2d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "What does the probit regression tell us? The positive coefficent (.0868) and statistically significant (z = 3.11, p = 0.002) which means **the treatment increased the liklihood of donation** \n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "_NOTE: Linear regression results appear replicate Table 3 column 1 in the paper. Probit results do not, despite Table 3 indicating its results come from probit regressions..._\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "### Differences between Match Rates\n",
        "\n",
        "Next, I assess the effectiveness of different sizes of matched donations on the response rate.\n",
        "\n",
        "_todo: Use a series of t-tests to test whether the size of the match ratio has an effect on whether people donate or not. For example, does the 2:1 match rate lead increase the likelihood that someone donates as compared to the 1:1 match rate? Do your results support the \"figures suggest\" comment the authors make on page 8?_\n",
        "\n",
        "#### T-Test Results"
      ],
      "id": "f5e22925"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#|echo: false\n",
        "# Filter to treatment group and drop missing values\n",
        "treat_df = df[(df['treatment'] == 1) & (df['ratio'].isin([1, 2, 3]))]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Subset donation outcomes by match ratio\n",
        "gave_1to1 = treat_df[treat_df['ratio'] == 1]['gave'].dropna()\n",
        "gave_2to1 = treat_df[treat_df['ratio'] == 2]['gave'].dropna()\n",
        "gave_3to1 = treat_df[treat_df['ratio'] == 3]['gave'].dropna()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Run pairwise t-tests\n",
        "from scipy.stats import ttest_ind\n",
        "\n",
        "ttest_1_2 = ttest_ind(gave_1to1, gave_2to1, equal_var=False)\n",
        "ttest_2_3 = ttest_ind(gave_2to1, gave_3to1, equal_var=False)\n",
        "ttest_1_3 = ttest_ind(gave_1to1, gave_3to1, equal_var=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Display results as a formatted table\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "\n",
        "t_test_results = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"Comparison\": [\"1:1 vs 2:1\", \"2:1 vs 3:1\", \"1:1 vs 3:1\"],\n",
        "    \"t-statistic\": [ttest_1_2.statistic, ttest_2_3.statistic, ttest_1_3.statistic],\n",
        "    \"p-value\": [ttest_1_2.pvalue, ttest_2_3.pvalue, ttest_1_3.pvalue]\n",
        "}).round(4)\n",
        "\n",
        "t_test_results"
      ],
      "id": "d7e4c616",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#### Regression on Explicit Match Ratio Dummies"
      ],
      "id": "a2a4e69b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "# Create dummy variables for match ratio (within treatment group only)\n",
        "treat_df = df[df['treatment'] == 1].copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "treat_df['ratio1'] = (treat_df['ratio'] == 1).astype(int)\n",
        "treat_df['ratio2'] = (treat_df['ratio'] == 2).astype(int)\n",
        "treat_df['ratio3'] = (treat_df['ratio'] == 3).astype(int)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Drop one to avoid multicollinearity – we'll drop ratio1 (1:1) so it becomes the reference group\n",
        "model = smf.ols('gave ~ ratio2 + ratio3', data=treat_df).fit()\n",
        "\n",
        "reg_table = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"Term\": [\"Intercept (1:1)\", \"2:1 vs 1:1\", \"3:1 vs 1:1\"],\n",
        "    \"Coefficient\": [model.params[\"Intercept\"], model.params[\"ratio2\"], model.params[\"ratio3\"]],\n",
        "    \"Std. Error\": [model.bse[\"Intercept\"], model.bse[\"ratio2\"], model.bse[\"ratio3\"]],\n",
        "    \"p-value\": [model.pvalues[\"Intercept\"], model.pvalues[\"ratio2\"], model.pvalues[\"ratio3\"]],\n",
        "    \"95% CI Lower\": [model.conf_int().loc[\"Intercept\", 0], model.conf_int().loc[\"ratio2\", 0], model.conf_int().loc[\"ratio3\", 0]],\n",
        "    \"95% CI Upper\": [model.conf_int().loc[\"Intercept\", 1], model.conf_int().loc[\"ratio2\", 1], model.conf_int().loc[\"ratio3\", 1]]\n",
        "}).round(4)\n",
        "\n",
        "reg_table"
      ],
      "id": "d95d2ab5",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The **intercept** coefficient (0.0207) represents the average donation rate for individuals who received a 1:1 match offer — approximately **2.07%** of these individuals made a donation.\n",
        "\n",
        "The coefficients for `ratio2` and `ratio3` estimate how much higher (or lower) the donation rate was for individuals who received 2:1 and 3:1 match offers, respectively:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **2:1 vs 1:1**: The coefficient of **0.0019** suggests a **0.19 percentage point increase** in the likelihood of donating relative to the 1:1 group.\n",
        "- **3:1 vs 1:1**: The coefficient of **0.0020** suggests a **0.20 percentage point increase** in donation probability compared to the 1:1 group.\n",
        "\n",
        "However, both of these estimates are **not statistically significant** (p-value > 0.05):\n",
        "\n",
        "These findings align with the original study's conclusion that **the presence of a match matters, but its size does not**.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "#### Response Rate Differences:"
      ],
      "id": "0484fdd1"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#|echo: false\n",
        "# Calculate response rates from the raw data\n",
        "rate_1to1 = gave_1to1.mean()\n",
        "rate_2to1 = gave_2to1.mean()\n",
        "rate_3to1 = gave_3to1.mean()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Compute differences directly\n",
        "diff_2_1 = rate_2to1 - rate_1to1\n",
        "diff_3_2 = rate_3to1 - rate_2to1\n",
        "\n",
        "# Display results\n",
        "print(f\"1:1 donation rate: {rate_1to1 * 100:.4f}%\")\n",
        "print(f\"2:1 donation rate: {rate_2to1 * 100:.4f}%\")\n",
        "print(f\"3:1 donation rate: {rate_3to1 * 100:.4f}%\")\n",
        "print(f\"Difference (2:1 - 1:1): {diff_2_1 * 100:.4f}%\")\n",
        "print(f\"Difference (3:1 - 2:1): {diff_3_2 * 100:.4f}%\")"
      ],
      "id": "04fcbe9b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#|echo: false\n",
        "# Use regression coefficients\n",
        "diff_reg_2_1 = model.params['ratio2']\n",
        "diff_reg_3_2 = model.params['ratio3'] - model.params['ratio2']\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Regression: Difference (2:1 - 1:1): {diff_reg_2_1*100:.4f}%\")\n",
        "print(f\"Regression: Difference (3:1 - 2:1): {diff_reg_3_2*100:.4f}%\")"
      ],
      "id": "9c2e9ae8",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "These results confirm that **moving from a 1:1 to a 2:1 or 3:1 match have very small, statistically insignificant effect**.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "### Size of Charitable Contribution\n",
        "\n",
        "In this subsection, I analyze the effect of the size of matched donation on the size of the charitable contribution.\n",
        "\n",
        "_todo: Calculate a t-test or run a bivariate linear regression of the donation amount on the treatment status. What do we learn from doing this analysis?_\n",
        "\n",
        "#### Unconditional Donation Amounts by Treatment Group"
      ],
      "id": "42606c5c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "# T-test: donation amount (includes zeros)\n",
